s.r.clarkstone@durham.ac.uk wrote:
>That seems a bit silly.  I imagine a minotaur as a fast creature, since 
>it charges at you.

Minotaurs are faster (speed 15) than "normal" speed (speed 12), but an
intrinsically fast player character has a time-averaged speed of 16 and
an extrinsically fast player character (!speed, haste self, speed boots)
character has a time-averaged speed of 20.

>(Also, the Vernon spoilers say "no random generation" too, but I am sure 
>I have encountered random ones.)

Minotaurs are never generated randomly at level generation or by the
"spawn random monsters out of sight at random intervals" generator.
However, they are a valid polymorph target.
